  "verdict": "ARGUMENTS AGAINST CONFOUNDING-BY-INDICATION: (a) E-value ~6 (CI ~5.5) on the severity-adjusted dose-response -> an unmeasured confounder would have to be implausibly strong; (b) the requirement->mortality OR stays >1 (CI excludes 1) in 8/8 within-severity strata (lactate quintiles + #vaso) -> the dose grades mortality even after CONDITIONING on the indication; (c) it persists within a homogeneous single-pressor/lactate-2-4 band (OR 1.464) and within sepsis (OR 3.519). Confounding by indication is not eliminated (observational) but is made IMPLAUSIBLE as the sole explanation. The IV + negative-control-exposure tests (separate module) are the remaining quasi-experimental checks."
